drm/amdgpu: no kernel mapping pointer for VRAM outside the visible window

amdgpu_ttm_io_mem_reserve hands TTM a premapped address, aper_base_kaddr
plus the resource offset, for any contiguous VRAM resource. aper_base_kaddr
maps only the CPU-visible part of VRAM (amdgpu_ttm_init ioremaps
visible_vram_size), so for a contiguous BO placed past it (a kernel BO
without AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_CPU_ACCESS_REQUIRED, which top-down placement
puts at the end of VRAM) ttm_bo_kmap and ttm_bo_vmap return a pointer past
the end of the mapping, and the first CPU store through it lands in
whatever follows. Give a premapped address only when the whole resource is
CPU visible (amdgpu_res_cpu_visible); otherwise TTM ioremaps the bus range,
which fails for VRAM past the BAR, and the kmap fails with an error.

On the dext, the pointer past the 256 MiB BAR0 mapping was treated as
process memory; a store through it crashed the driver process, and a dext
that dies with its PCI session open panics the Mac (IOPCIFamily crash
recovery). The upstream behaviour for visible VRAM is unchanged.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
index 3d2e00e..4cc6ba7 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
@@ -633,8 +633,10 @@ static int amdgpu_ttm_io_mem_reserve(struct ttm_device *bdev,
 	case TTM_PL_VRAM:
 		mem->bus.offset = mem->start << PAGE_SHIFT;
 
+		/* The kernel mapping covers the CPU-visible window only. */
 		if (adev->mman.aper_base_kaddr &&
-		    mem->placement & TTM_PL_FLAG_CONTIGUOUS)
+		    mem->placement & TTM_PL_FLAG_CONTIGUOUS &&
+		    amdgpu_res_cpu_visible(adev, mem))
 			mem->bus.addr = (u8 *)adev->mman.aper_base_kaddr +
 					mem->bus.offset;
 
